+field-extraction type boundary, not full Pipfile validation, manager execution,
+proof of install rejection or proof that a hidden exact pin exists.
+
+Inspect only values actually traversed by the existing `_parse_pipfile` loop
+in the existing `packages` and `dev-packages` mappings, after successful TOML
+decoding and existing section checks. This is one helper call site traversing
+two sections. A value triggers exactly when it is a dict, contains the raw key
+`version`, and its `version` value is not a str. Check presence and type before
+truthiness fallback; false, zero, numeric values, wrong-type empty containers
+and TOML date/time values qualify. TOML has no decoded null. Transport plus an
+explicit non-string version qualifies solely by this field predicate, without
+asserting transport precedence, installer behavior or recoverable exact credit.
